  "_taxonomy": "31 segments, named the way the US technical-textiles trade names them (marine, awnings, transit interiors, technical textiles...) rather than the way ACT's free-text field grew. Broad enough to be recognisable to anyone in the industry, narrow enough that two genuinely different trades - marine and automotive, awnings and tents - never share a row.",
  "_aliases": "Every raw ACT spelling mapped to its segment, plus the intermediate cleaned names so an earlier import of those can be merged in. null marks a value that is not an industry at all (NIL, Poor info, prospect - 307 rows). Keys are matched case-insensitively and trimmed by the importer, so a stray 'APPAREL' still resolves. This is the map the ACT contact import will need: a contact's raw Industry text resolves through here to a row the importer created.",
